  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TB Local Organisations Network (TB-LON/KNTB)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Zimbabwe):  .A network of local organizations implements the Tuberculosis (TB) Local Organizations Network (TB-LON) activity in support of the National Tuberculosis Program (NTP). TB-LON assists the NTP to design, develop, and implement policies, strategies, and services that support the prevention of TB transmission, increase the detection of TB cases, link identified cases into care and treatment, support positive treatment outcomes, and create an enabling environment for TB control in Zimbabwe. ..With FY 2022 funds, TB-LON will provide technical assistance to the MOHCC for the following:..- Implementing national TB policies, strategies, and guidelines;- Improving TB case-finding from all sources; - Building the capacity of NTP personnel on effective program management and quality data use; - Providing TB and HIV clinical services in health facilities and in communities; - Supporting health systems and service delivery platforms for quality TB services;- Documenting the burden of multidrug-resistant TB (MDR-TB);  - Implementing evidence-based diagnosis, management, and prevention interventions to control MDR-TB; and- Controlling silico-TB (co-existence of silicosis and tuberculosis)...These interventions will result in improved TB prevention, case detection, case management, and the creation of a more sustainable, enabling environment for TB control in Zimbabwe. Further, FY 2023 funds will support increased capacity for local organizations to implement TB control activities and enable greater geographic coverage, from the current eight districts to twelve....</narrative>
  </description>
